  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Sarah and Trang have $\\$36$ between them. Sarah gives Trang $\\$2$, but then still has twice as much as Trang. How much money did they each originally have?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Sarah had $\\$26$ and Trang had $\\$10$.",
      "worked": "Let Sarah originally have $x$ dollars and Trang $y$ dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=36\\\\x-2&=2(y+2)\\\\x&=36-y\\\\36-y-2&=2(y+2)\\\\34-y&=2y+4\\\\30&=3y\\\\y&=10\\\\x&=36-10\\\\x&=26\\end{align*}$$\n\nSarah originally had $\\$26$ and Trang had $\\$10$. After the transfer, they have $\\$24$ and $\\$12$, respectively, and $24=2\\times12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
